{
  "id": "ZEP.3",
  "number": "3",
  "bookId": "ZEP",
  "reference": "Zephaniah 3",
  "verseCount": 20,
  "content": [
    {
      "name": "chapter",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "number": "3",
        "style": "c",
        "sid": "ZEP 3"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "text": "3",
          "type": "text"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "1",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ZEP 3:1"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "1",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Woe to her that is rebellious and polluted! to the oppressing city! ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ZEP.3.1",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ZEP.3.1"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "2",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ZEP 3:2"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "2",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "She obeyed not the voice; she received not correction; she trusted not in Jehovah; she drew not near to her God. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ZEP.3.2",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ZEP.3.2"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "3",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ZEP 3:3"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "3",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Her princes in the midst of her are roaring lions; her judges are evening wolves; they leave nothing till the morrow. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ZEP.3.3",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ZEP.3.3"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "4",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ZEP 3:4"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "4",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Her prophets are light and treacherous persons; her priests have profaned the sanctuary, they have done violence to the law. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ZEP.3.4",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ZEP.3.4"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "5",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ZEP 3:5"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "5",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Jehovah in the midst of her is righteous; he will not do iniquity; every morning doth he bring his justice to light, he faileth not; but the unjust knoweth no shame. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ZEP.3.5",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ZEP.3.5"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "6",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ZEP 3:6"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "6",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "I have cut off nations; their battlements are desolate; I have made their streets waste, so that none passeth by; their cities are destroyed, so that there is no man, so that there is no inhabitant. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ZEP.3.6",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ZEP.3.6"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "7",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ZEP 3:7"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "7",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "I said, Only fear thou me; receive correction; so her dwelling shall not be cut off, ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ZEP.3.7",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ZEP.3.7"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " all that I have appointed concerning her: but they rose early and corrupted all their doings.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ZEP.3.7",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ZEP.3.7"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "7",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ZEP 3:7"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "7",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ZEP.3.7",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ZEP.3.7"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "8",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ZEP 3:8"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "8",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Therefore wait ye for me, saith Jehovah, until the day that I rise up to the prey; for my determination is to gather the nations, that I may assemble the kingdoms, to pour upon them mine indignation, even all my fierce anger; for all the earth shall be devoured with the fire of my jealousy.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ZEP.3.8",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ZEP.3.8"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "8",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ZEP 3:8"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "8",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ZEP.3.8",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ZEP.3.8"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "9",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ZEP 3:9"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "9",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "For then will I turn to the peoples of a pure language, that they may all call upon the name of Jehovah, to serve him with one consent. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ZEP.3.9",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ZEP.3.9"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "10",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ZEP 3:10"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "10",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "From beyond the rivers of Ethiopia my suppliants, even the daughter of my dispersed, shall bring mine offering. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ZEP.3.10",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ZEP.3.10"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "11",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ZEP 3:11"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "11",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "In that day shalt thou not be put to shame for all thy doings, wherein thou hast transgressed against me; for then I will take away out of the midst of thee thy proudly exulting ones, and thou shalt no more be haughty in my holy mountain. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ZEP.3.11",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ZEP.3.11"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "12",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ZEP 3:12"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "12",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "But I will leave in the midst of thee an afflicted and poor people, and they shall take refuge in the name of Jehovah. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ZEP.3.12",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ZEP.3.12"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "13",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ZEP 3:13"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "13",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The remnant of Israel shall not do iniquity, nor speak lies; neither shall a deceitful tongue be found in their mouth; for they shall feed and lie down, and none shall make them afraid.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ZEP.3.13",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ZEP.3.13"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "13",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ZEP 3:13"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "13",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ZEP.3.13",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ZEP.3.13"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "14",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ZEP 3:14"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "14",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Sing, O daughter of Zion; shout, O Israel; be glad and rejoice with all the heart, O daughter of Jerusalem. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ZEP.3.14",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ZEP.3.14"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "15",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ZEP 3:15"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "15",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Jehovah hath taken away thy judgments, he hath cast out thine enemy: the King of Israel, even Jehovah, is in the midst of thee; thou shalt not fear evil any more. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ZEP.3.15",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ZEP.3.15"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "16",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ZEP 3:16"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "16",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "In that day it shall be said to Jerusalem, Fear thou not; O Zion, let not thy hands be slack. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ZEP.3.16",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ZEP.3.16"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "17",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ZEP 3:17"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "17",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Jehovah thy God is in the midst of thee, a mighty one who will save; he will rejoice over thee with joy; he will rest in his love; he will joy over thee with singing. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ZEP.3.17",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ZEP.3.17"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "18",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ZEP 3:18"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "18",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "I will gather them that sorrow for the solemn assembly, who were of thee; ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ZEP.3.18",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ZEP.3.18"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " the burden upon her was a reproach. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ZEP.3.18",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ZEP.3.18"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "19",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ZEP 3:19"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "19",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Behold, at that time I will deal with all them that afflict thee; and I will save that which is lame, and gather that which was driven away; and I will make them a praise and a name, whose shame hath been in all the earth. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ZEP.3.19",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ZEP.3.19"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "20",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ZEP 3:20"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "20",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "At that time will I bring you in, and at that time will I gather you; for I will make you a name and a praise among all the peoples of the earth, when I bring back your captivity before your eyes, saith Jehovah.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ZEP.3.20",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ZEP.3.20"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
